(in-package #:bitcoin-lisp.cli)

;;;; Command-line arguments to JSON-RPC params (Core rpc/client.cpp)
;;;
;;; bitcoin-cli sends every argument as a JSON STRING unless the table below
;;; says the (method, position) or (method, name) is JSON. Nothing else
;;; decides it -- not the argument's shape, not the server's declared types --
;;; so `bitcoin-cli getblockhash 5' works only because the table lists
;;; getblockhash's height, and `bitcoin-cli echo 1' sends the string "1".
;;; The rows are Core's vRPCConvertParams at the project pin (d3056bc149,
;;; rpc/client.cpp:57-393), transcribed mechanically, in Core's order: the
;;; lookups are first-match, like Core's std::ranges::find_if. This is NOT the
;;; server's *RPC-ARG-CONVERSIONS* (src/rpc/core-tables.lisp), which comes from
;;; the RPCHelpMan declarations and cannot say JSON-or-string; Core keeps the
;;; two apart as well, and rpc_help.py compares them.

